      "role": "user",
      "content": "yo, i've been looking at the orbital decay data for the decommissioned clusters in sector 4, specifically the drift vectors from the 17th. something's not right. the delta-v deviations aren't following a standard gravitational decay curve. i've logged these specific drift offsets: 0.11, 0.44, 0.22, 0.88, 0.33, 0.66. it looks like they're pulsing or adjusting. do u see a pattern in those numbers? it feels like it's more of a systematic shift than just random orbital perturbation.",
